# Build output
build/
# Side-by-side build trees, e.g. build-nocuda/ for the --no-cuda configuration that
# CI's first job uses.  This existed and was NOT covered by the rule above, so a
# `git add -A` would have committed a whole second build tree.  The suffix form is
# deliberate: `build/` alone is what let that happen.
build-*/
build*/
out/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored dependencies -- NOT part of rdither, and enormous
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FFmpeg-master/ is 10,772 files and 88 MB of someone else's project, unpacked
# alongside the source for reference.  OpenCL-SDK-* is the Khronos SDK, which
# CMakeLists.txt auto-detects beside the tree.  Both are third-party, both are
# re-obtainable from their own projects, and committing either would bury this
# repository's own history under theirs.
#
# The README says where each comes from and that the build expects them beside
# the source rather than inside it.
/FFmpeg-master/
/OpenCL-SDK-*/

# Probe binaries.  tools\probe_swscale_matrix.cpp is tracked; its .exe is not,
# because a 220 KB binary in a source tree is the kind of thing that gets
# committed by accident and then conflicts on every branch.  Rebuild it from
# the .cpp.  The scripts under tools\ are tracked -- they are the record of how
# the measurements were taken, which is the part worth keeping.
*.exe

# Rendered clips and scratch frames
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.nut
n.mkv
o.mkv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test fixtures
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tests/ splits into three kinds of file, and only one of them belongs in git.
#
#   INPUTS      in_*.png, noisy.png, t_*.png, c*.png, g*.png  -- the images
#               verify.ps1 builds its cases from.  Tracked, because the test
#               suite is the thing worth reproducing.
#
#   OUTPUTS     *_ref.png, *_cpu.png, *_cuda.png, *_cpu_disk.png -- regenerated
#               by every verify.ps1 run and by probe-opencl-exact.ps1.  180
#               files, ~5 MB, and they are stale the moment anything changes.
#               Tracked, they turn every measurement into a spurious diff.
#
#   LEFTOVERS   fhd.png, fhd_photo.png, big.png, smooth.png -- 23 MB of large
#               images that no test, script or source file references at all
#               (checked: zero hits across verify.ps1, tools\*.ps1 and src\).
#               Not committed, and regenerable from the same ImageMagick calls
#               the fixtures use.
*_ref.png
*_cpu.png
*_cuda.png
*_cpu_disk.png
tests/fhd.png
tests/fhd_photo.png
tests/big.png
tests/smooth.png

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.vs/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Hi-res source photographs for the README showcase.  Regenerate from the
# Wikimedia Commons URLs recorded in docs/examples/SOURCES.md; the dithered
# outputs in docs/examples/ are what gets committed.
*.orig.jpg
